"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-2/trig-omp-reported/8/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Python 3.13 \u2192 `datetime.fromisoformat` accepts `Z` (3.11+), keeps naive inputs naive, and returns aware UTC for `Z`/offset inputs.\nI fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` by replacing `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. The old format string had no way to match a trailing `Z`, so it raised the error. On Python 3.11 and later (this repo runs 3.13.5), `fromisoformat` understands `Z` and numeric offsets like `+02:00`. `pytest tests/test_parse.py` now passes all 3 tests, including `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nOne behaviour change: a timestamp ending in `Z` or an offset now comes back timezone-aware (UTC for `Z`). Previously it raised an error, so no working code depended on that. Timestamps without a suffix still come back without a timezone. The only other caller is `day_key`, which just formats the date and isn't affected.\n\nThe risk is mixing the two kinds later: comparing or subtracting a timezone-aware and a timezone-free datetime raises `TypeError`. If anything downstream does that, either convert timezone-aware values to UTC and strip the zone, or make timezone-free values UTC.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 77328, "requests_cache_write": 105947, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5689846, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 1186, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-reported:claude-opus-5-5:trial8", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 14, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T22:46:28.268719+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 27.609, "t_checker_s": 0.325, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-reported", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1202, "tokens_cache_read": 77328, "tokens_cache_write": 105947, "tokens_fresh": 1202, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 77328, "tokens_main_cache_write": 105947, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 1186, "tokens_output": 1186, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 77328, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 105947, "tokens_proxy_calls": 7, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 1186, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 8, "ts_iso": "2026-10-17T18:46:28", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 7, "upstream_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage_raw": [{"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 25190, "cost": {"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "input": 0, "output": 0, "total": 0}, "cttl": {"ephemeral5m": 25190}, "input": 4, "output": 87, "totalTokens": 25281}, {"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 25492, "cost": {"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "i